{
  "page": 8,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (05/2025)",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        27.39893913269043,
        368.4171447753906,
        37.36153793334961
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We then replaced the trained value model with a novel objective Vn for scoring and ranking trajectories in",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        83.85389709472656,
        540.0933227539062,
        95.31149291992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our planning loop, using fnovel(st, At) = 5 exp(−(ht −htarget)2/2σ2), where ht is the dimension of the state",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        95.35905456542969,
        540.064208984375,
        107.26657104492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "st that corresponds to the height of the agent, htarget is the target height, σ2 = 5 × 10−4, κ = 0 and ˜κ = 1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        104.14888000488281,
        540.9979248046875,
        119.22152709960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(so we only use the new ˜J and ignore the original J). By using this simple method, we were able to make",
      "bbox": [
        70.83399963378906,
        117.20191955566406,
        540.08349609375,
        129.68252563476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the agent lunge forward and keep its head down (htarget = 0.9), balance itself (htarget = 1.2), and repeatedly",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        131.67494201660156,
        540.4093627929688,
        143.13156127929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "jump (htarget = 1.4). Note that for the experiments presented in Fig. 1, we utilize a pure novel reward setting",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        143.62989807128906,
        540.1918334960938,
        155.08749389648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by setting κ = 0 and ˜κ = 1. This means the value function used for planning, Vn, is solely determined",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        155.5849151611328,
        540.0549926757812,
        166.4029083251953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by the novel reward function, ˜J. The original reward function, J, derived from the pre-training data, has",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        165.0219268798828,
        540.0838623046875,
        177.50350952148438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "no influence on the agent’s behavior in these cases. The resulting lunge, balance, and jump behaviors are",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        179.4959259033203,
        540.2583618164062,
        189.45852661132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "therefore direct consequences of optimizing ˜J and are not present in the original dataset.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        188.9329376220703,
        460.3165283203125,
        201.41354370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We also compared D-MPC with Diffuser on these novel reward tasks. Diffuser can also optimize these rewards,",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        209.38392639160156,
        541.5877075195312,
        219.34652709960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and we did not observe a significant performance difference. However, D-MPC’s key advantage lies in its",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        221.3389434814453,
        540.2174682617188,
        231.30154418945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ability to adapt to novel dynamics, as discussed in Section 4.3.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        233.2938995361328,
        345.8320007324219,
        243.25650024414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
